WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.100
-I'm excited to see you.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.133
It's interesting.
In your intro there,

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:04.734
it kind of changed from earlier,

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:06.834
but I introduced you
as America's sweetheart.

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:08.400
Is that --
-Well, I just did a movie

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.801
with Reese Witherspoon,
Anna Kendrick, and Ashton Kutcher.

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:13.968
-Wow.
[ Cheers ]

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:16.334
-And I think
we all saw it coming.

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:17.968
But --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.968 --> 00:00:20.501
At one point,
somebody referred to Reese

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:23.033
as America's sweetheart,
and she didn't take

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:26.000
that title on, and I just --

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.067
I told her,
"Well, I guess I'll take it."

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:30.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:33.434
-We always love when you come
to visit us,

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:35.300
and you brought us something
interesting to me.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.834
This is --
You've been on the road.

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:38.567
You're doing your tour,
"Hello Again."

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:40.100
I just want to give it
a little quick plug.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.667
Pittsburgh, Cleveland, Detroit,
Columbus, Ithaca, Boston,

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:47.501
Washington, Philly, Portland,
San Francisco, New Orleans...

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:49.901
-New Orleans, Chicago, Madison.
-Chicago, Madison, Wisconsin.

00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:51.567
New York, New York.
-New York City, yeah.

00:00:51.567 --> 00:00:53.467
-This is a big tour.
That's a big tour.

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:55.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
-There's even more.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.334
I think there's 40 dates.
Those are just --

00:00:57.334 --> 00:00:59.000
-Wow!
Some dates right there.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.234
-Yeah, those are some.
-But you've been travelling

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:02.767
a lot,
and you've had some experiences.

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:03.901
Let's just say that.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:05.667
-At the airport.
And you've taken photos,

00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:07.167
and you've brought the photos
to our show.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:09.901
-Yes.
-And can I show the photo first

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:11.968
or do you want to talk about
the situation?

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:14.234
-Well, I'll tell you, you know,

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:16.968
we are in the middle
of a pandemic.

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:22.133
And I was in between cities,
and I was hungry.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:27.467
And so, I scoured the airport
for a place to sit alone,

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:30.634
away from everyone
to be as safe as I could

00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:32.734
to take my mask off and eat.
-Yeah.

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:36.501
-And I laid out all of my food
on the seat next to me.

00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:38.968
And right as I started eating --

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:42.601
and I'm telling you,
the area was empty.

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:45.467
Show the picture.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:47.868
These are all empty seats.

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:50.501
So are these.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:53.667
So are across from her.
-But right behind --

00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:56.901
-So was the whole row
that she was sitting in.

00:01:56.901 --> 00:01:59.701
But she sat right there,
right behind me.

00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:02.634
-This other photo is something
that we can all help you with.

00:02:02.634 --> 00:02:05.434
You brought us --
You brought us a problem

00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:07.868
that we can give you a solution.
-I'm hoping.

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:11.567
Here's the thing is, I don't
follow a lot of pop culture,

00:02:11.567 --> 00:02:14.133
and I'll be fair, you know,
and honest and say,

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:17.734
I'm not great at recognizing
a lot of celebrities...

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:20.234
-Yes.
-...because I don't follow

00:02:20.234 --> 00:02:22.167
a lot of pop culture.

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:23.367
-But you're America's
sweetheart.

00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:24.834
-I am America's sweetheart.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.834 --> 00:02:27.100
-Yeah, yeah.
-People follow what I'm doing.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:28.501
-People follow --
Oh, I understand.

00:02:28.501 --> 00:02:31.467
-Yeah.
-Of course.

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:32.801
Of course.
That's what they do, yeah.

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:35.667
[ Applause ]
-Another standing ovation.

00:02:35.667 --> 00:02:38.334
So, I was sitting
on this flight,

00:02:38.334 --> 00:02:43.000
and everybody that walked on
kept saying to the woman

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.901
next to me, "Oh, my gosh.

00:02:44.901 --> 00:02:48.968
I'd know that face from anywhere
or even with a mask on.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.267
Look at you.
I know that hair."

00:02:51.267 --> 00:02:53.234
And I was like,
"Who the hell is this?"

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:54.968
[ Laughter ]
And, of course,

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:58.467
she had a mask on,
and so I snuck a picture

00:02:58.467 --> 00:03:01.000
and sent it to my wife,
and I was like, "Who is this?"

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.701
And then, she didn't know.
And then we sent it

00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:05.734
to everyone else that was
celebrity-obsessed.

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:08.033
Nobody knows who this person is.

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:09.400
-And you didn't
want to ask the person.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.267
You're not --
-Well, no, halfway through

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:13.601
the flight,
there was a spider on her leg,

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:15.067
and, uh...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.067 --> 00:03:19.667
And I said, "Oh, excuse me.
You have a spider on your leg."

00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:21.968
And she said, "Oh, my gosh.
Thank you."

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.634
And she brushed it off.

00:03:23.634 --> 00:03:25.667
And I was like,
"I don't know that voice."

00:03:25.667 --> 00:03:28.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:29.133
"Who is this person?"
-All right.

00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:30.701
So you brought the photo.
-Yeah.

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:33.200
-And this is the person
that was sitting next to you.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:37.334
And do we know who this?
-Who is that?

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:41.234
Please, call 1-800...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:44.534
-Let me see this here.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.534 --> 00:03:48.901
-And whoever she is,
please don't be upset with me.

00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:51.334
-She has red hair.
-And a widow's peak.

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:53.567
-Is it Debra Messing?
-No.

00:03:53.567 --> 00:03:55.701
I feel like Deborah and I
would --

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.801 --> 00:04:02.167
Let me look at this.
-Yeah.

00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:03.601
I have no clue.
Jenna Fischer?

00:04:03.601 --> 00:04:05.968
-It's America's sweetheart.
-What?

00:04:05.968 --> 00:04:07.968
No, no, no, it's not.
-No, no.

00:04:07.968 --> 00:04:09.834
-No, it's not Jenna Fischer.
-She's very pretty.

00:04:09.834 --> 00:04:11.567
Very pretty.
She looks like she's married.

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:13.200
That's a wedding ring.
-Yeah.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.734
-So she's married.
-She carries a yellow bag.

00:04:15.734 --> 00:04:19.901
-A yellow bag.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:21.868
This last one is --

00:04:21.868 --> 00:04:23.901
I don't even know
if you want to even set this up.

00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:25.734
I'm just gonna show the picture.
-Well, I do want to say,

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:28.567
this person wasn't --
-It's a tough situation.

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:31.734
-It wasn't that she was mean.
She just wasn't

00:04:31.734 --> 00:04:34.901
terribly friendly when we
sat next to each other.

00:04:34.901 --> 00:04:36.634
And I thought,
"Well, I'm not gonna be

00:04:36.634 --> 00:04:41.334
mean back, but this is..."
-Okay. Here's the photo.

00:04:41.334 --> 00:04:43.667
Here's the photo.
We blurred her face out.

00:04:43.667 --> 00:04:46.200
Here's the photo.
This actually happened to you.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:49.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:51.167
What in the world?

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:54.133
-Well, you know what?
-What in the world happens

00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:57.367
in your life
where this happens in your life?

00:04:57.367 --> 00:04:58.901
-I was sitting there.

00:04:58.901 --> 00:05:01.234
And this was obviously
pre-pandemic.

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:06.033
And we had our masks off, and
I started to see this happen,

00:05:06.033 --> 00:05:08.367
and I was like,
"Oh, boy. Uh-oh."

00:05:08.367 --> 00:05:10.567
[ Laughter ]
"Somebody's sleepy."

00:05:10.567 --> 00:05:14.434
And then, she went down.

00:05:14.434 --> 00:05:16.501
And she was rest--

00:05:16.501 --> 00:05:18.901
She was snuggled
into my shoulder.

00:05:18.901 --> 00:05:20.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.133 --> 00:05:21.367
-You didn't say anything?
You didn't wake her up?

00:05:21.367 --> 00:05:23.667
-No. I let her sleep
the whole flight.

00:05:23.667 --> 00:05:26.334
-Wow.
I want to, once again,

00:05:26.334 --> 00:05:29.300
talk about -- you're on tour
starting January 11th.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.734
-Yeah, "Hello Again"
is the name of the tour.

00:05:31.734 --> 00:05:35.000
And it sounds obvious,
because there is

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.667
the obvious reason
of, "Hello, again.

00:05:36.667 --> 00:05:39.300
I haven't toured
in a couple of years."

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:44.367
But there's another reason
that it's called "Hello Again."

00:05:44.367 --> 00:05:46.334
I'm not gonna tell you why.
-Yeah, I know.

00:05:46.334 --> 00:05:48.767
That's what
makes you very interesting.

00:05:48.767 --> 00:05:52.167
You told me that to find out
why it's called "Hello Again"

00:05:52.167 --> 00:05:55.200
that I have to see the tour
and find out.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.467
-The whole tour.
You have to buy tickets.

00:05:57.467 --> 00:06:00.367
-No, no, no, no.
But at the end of your act,

00:06:00.367 --> 00:06:02.467
you understand why it's called
"Hello Again."

00:06:02.467 --> 00:06:07.501
-Yes, and it's a very fun moment
that you don't want to miss.

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:10.100
[ Laughter ]
-Tig Notaro, everybody!

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:11.467 --> 00:06:14.000
For more information
on her "Hello Again" tour,

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.534
go to tignotaro.com.

00:06:16.534 --> 00:06:18.801
-America's sweetheart.
-America's sweetheart.

